From 1f50d704a9d543d2d6bb862d8a6ed3e321354178 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:43:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] docs(site): say what the browser version opens and saves

The front page and the First run page said that the browser version
cannot open or save files. Since v0.20.0 it opens a model or a project
with the browser's file picker (#1314), and Save, Save As and Post
download (#1438). The pages now say this, and name the file commands
that the browser version still refuses (crates/ui/src/browser_files.rs).

Fixes #1833

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 site/content/guide/first-run.md | 10 +++++++---
 site/templates/index.html       |  7 +++++--
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/site/content/guide/first-run.md b/site/content/guide/first-run.md
index 366f0ab6f..fd5676ca5 100644
--- a/site/content/guide/first-run.md
+++ b/site/content/guide/first-run.md
@@ -10,9 +10,13 @@ When this site's release has a browser version,
 [CamCraft in the browser](@/app.md) opens it with nothing to install (it
 needs a browser with WebGL2: a current Chrome, Firefox, Edge or Safari), so
 you can look around the window described below; if it does not, that page
-says so, and the front page says which it is. The browser version cannot
-open or save files yet and simulation playback does not work in it, so for a
-real first toolpath, install a [desktop build](@/guide/install.md).
+says so, and the front page says which it is. The browser version opens a
+model or a project with the browser's file picker, and Save, Save As and Post
+download the project and the program. Its other file commands (recent files,
+machine, post, theme, fixture and tool library files, and the setup sheet,
+tool list and stock exports) are greyed and say why, and simulation playback
+does not work in it, so for real work, install a
+[desktop build](@/guide/install.md).
 
 ## The window
 
diff --git a/site/templates/index.html b/site/templates/index.html
index f5da07f15..275732dc7 100644
--- a/site/templates/index.html
+++ b/site/templates/index.html
@@ -28,8 +28,11 @@ <h2>Try CamCraft in your browser</h2>
     copy of this site; this local preview does not have it.</p>
   {% endif %}
   <p>
-    The browser version is an early one. It cannot open or save files yet (models,
-    projects and programs), simulation playback does not work in it yet, it does not use
+    The browser version is an early one. It opens a model or a project with the
+    browser's file picker, and Save, Save As and Post download the project and the
+    program. Other file commands are greyed and say why: recent files, loading a
+    machine, post, theme, fixture or tool library, and exporting a setup sheet, tool
+    list or stock model. Simulation playback does not work in it yet, it does not use
     the newer WebGPU graphics, and views that need more graphics features than the
     browser offers say so instead of drawing. For real work, use the
     <a href="{{ config.extra.repo }}/releases">desktop downloads</a>

